//! **A composable `FederationDirectory` double (CIRISPersist#603/#604).**
//!
//! GENERATED by `scripts/gen_directory_double.py`. Do not edit by hand —
//! edit the generator. `scripts/gen_directory_double.py --check` fails if this
//! file is stale.
//!
//! # The arm nobody could reach
//!
//! `resolve_mesh_config` folds per-root reads and carries `unreadable_roots`,
//! so *"this backend cannot answer for root R"* and *"root R said nothing"* stay
//! distinct. **No test in this repo could reach that arm**: all three shipped
//! backends implement every method, so none can return `Error::Unsupported`.
//! The only party exercising it was CIRISServer, through their own directory
//! impl — which is how the defect was found in the first place (#603).
//!
//! #604 recorded the pattern across five workstreams in one week:
//!
//! ```text
//! Ok(value)  -> a real answer
//! Ok(empty)  -> a real answer that happens to be empty
//! Err(_)     -> WE COULD NOT ASK
//! ```
//!
//! Collapsing that third arm is how a zero becomes evidence it has not earned.
//! The Constitution's own discipline: **a zero is not evidence unless the
//! instrument can fail.** This is the instrument that can fail.
//!
//! # Shape
//!
//! It WRAPS a real directory rather than stubbing 162 methods, so every
//! un-faulted call keeps real behaviour and a fixture only declares the
//! divergence it cares about.
//!
//! ```ignore
//! let dbl = FaultInjectingDirectory::new(backend)
//!     .unsupported("list_attestations_for");
//! // every other method behaves exactly as `backend` does
//! ```
//!
//! Test-only: `#[cfg(any(test, feature = "test-anchor"))]`, and `pub` because
//! CIRISServer/Edge/Agent need it (#664 was the same wall one module over).

// A glob import on purpose: this file delegates EVERY trait signature, so it
// needs the trait's whole type scope. Naming them individually would be a
// second list to keep in sync with the first — the exact failure this
// generator exists to remove.
